      "profile": "SP-18",
      "question": "I'm on the structural side of a big federated job and found the passage pasted below in the Project Info docs. When I open our IFC, how do I switch that on so I can limit what comes in to the structural classes such as columns, and what do I press once the filter is set?",
      "reference": {
        "answer": {
          "support": ["C1.Q4", "C3.Q1", "C1.Q1", "C2.Q1", "C2.Q2", "C1.Q2", "C1.Q5"],
          "text": "That is the Advanced Loading Mode, which can be particularly helpful when working with large and complex IFC models. Load the IFC with File > Open IFC Project and click the Enable Advanced Mode checkbox when loading; the model is preloaded and the Project Info panel presents the loading options. Choose the IFC Class filter mode, which filters by IFC class such as Wall or Column, then click the Load Project Elements button to load the filtered model."
        },
        "assumptions": ["blender", "bonsai", "model_state"],
        "hazard": null,
        "scope_note": {
          "support": ["C1.Q3", "C2.Q2"],
          "text": "The docs list the filter modes but do not describe the settings inside each mode, so pick the classes using the options the panel presents."
        },
        "steps": [
          {
            "support": ["C3.Q1", "C1.Q1"],
            "text": "Load the IFC with File > Open IFC Project, and click the Enable Advanced Mode checkbox when loading it."
          },
          {
            "support": ["C2.Q1", "C1.Q3"],
            "text": "Bonsai preloads the model and presents the loading options in the Project Info panel."
          },
          {
            "support": ["C2.Q2", "C2.Q3"],
            "text": "Choose the IFC Class filter mode, which filters by IFC class such as Wall or Column; Whitelist or Blacklist instead lets you type a custom query."
          },
          {
            "support": ["C1.Q5", "C1.Q2"],
            "text": "Once the desired settings have been configured, click the Load Project Elements button to load the filtered model."
          }
        ],
        "tools": [
          {"display": "Load Project Elements", "kind": "bonsai_operator", "value": "bim.load_project_elements"},
          {"display": "Load Project", "kind": "bonsai_operator", "value": "bim.load_project"}
        ]
      },
      "review": {"decided_on": "2026-11-22", "decision_id": "GP-004.06", "packet_id": "GP-004", "reviewed_draft_sha256": "b2a9f6f2f9590a503306f5397feec06d56979599f5ba3f98f0c2e22a7e1e50b0", "setup_sha256": "a4b34dfaf5770173382985de72db6c959435a300dbbf7e2e96a005e857249c33", "status": "chad_accepted", "words": "approve"},
